IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- PART 12ZE, STATUTORY NEONATAL CARE PAY, ss 171ZZ16 to 171ZZ24 (src:4130-4251).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The source is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- ss 171ZZ17-171ZZ24 are derived from the 12ZD source by work/tr_ze.py after a line-by-line diff of the two texts;
-- ss 171ZZ16 (this head) is hand-written because it differs.
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29):
--   JUST FALSE / JUST TRUE : the text says no / yes in its own words (each "no" branch quotes them).
--   NOTHING                : not covered (each branch says why: silent, list not closed, includes,
--                            undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling.  Rates, periods and lengths that regulations supply are
-- INPUTS.  Dates are `Date day month year`.

§ `Part 12ZE -- Statutory neonatal care pay`

§§ `s 171ZZ16 Entitlement`

-- Nouns.  The facts of the person's case that s 171ZZ16(2) and (3) read.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case` HAS
    `the employment`                          IS AN Employment
    `the child's date of birth`               IS A DATE
    `the day the neonatal care started`       IS A DATE
    `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of uninterrupted care`      IS A DATE
    `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to a parental or other personal relationship with the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`                      IS A NUMBER
    `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week`    IS A NUMBER
    `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- Nouns for s 171ZZ16(6): which entitlement the person has in respect of the child.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` HAS
    `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) The grant.  "A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) and any condition prescribed under subsection (3)
-- is entitled".  A failed "who satisfies" is counted as the text's no (reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- Regulations under s 171ZZ17(4) may modify or disapply conditions: if one does, the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4132 | (1) A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) and any condition prescribed under subsection (3) is entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory neonatal care pay”.
@ref s 171ZZ16(1) (src:4132)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
      `s 171ZZ17(4) regulations modify or disapply a condition in the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` MEANS
    IF `s 171ZZ17(4) regulations modify or disapply a condition in the person's case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZZ17(4)(c) and (d) let regulations modify the conditions or say that (2)(c) has no effect
    ELSE IF NOT (    `s 171ZZ16(2) the conditions are satisfied`
                       facts
                       `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
                       `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`
                 AND (`s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied`
                       (facts's `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)`)
                       (facts's `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment`)
                       (facts's `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week`)
                      EQUALS JUST TRUE))
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) and any condition prescribed under subsection (3) is entitled" (a failed condition; reading (a))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) The conditions: (a)(i) and (a)(ii) about the child's care, then (b), (c) and (d).
-- src:4133 | (2) The conditions are—
-- src:4134 | (a) that—
-- src:4135 | (i) the person satisfies prescribed conditions as to a parental or other personal relationship with a child who is receiving, or has received, neonatal care, and
-- src:4136 | (ii) that care continues without interruption for a period of at least seven days beginning with the day after the day on which the care starts,
-- src:4137 | (b) that the person has been in employed earner’s employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week,
-- src:4138 | (c) that at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7)), and
-- src:4139 | (d) that the person’s normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week.
@ref s 171ZZ16(2) (src:4133-4139)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(2) the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
        (facts's `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to a parental or other personal relationship with the child`)
    AND `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care`
          (facts's `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind`)
          (facts's `the day the neonatal care started`)
          (facts's `the child's date of birth`)
        EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) the care has continued without interruption for at least seven days`
          (facts's `the day the neonatal care started`)
          (facts's `the last day of uninterrupted care`)
    AND `s 171ZZ16(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks`
          (facts's `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`)
    AND `s 171ZZ16(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment`
          (facts's `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment`)
          (`s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (facts's `the day the neonatal care started`) `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`)
    AND `s 171ZZ16(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit`
          (facts's `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week`)
          `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`

-- (2)(a)(ii) "that care continues without interruption for a period of at least seven days beginning with the day after
-- the day on which the care starts."  The period begins the day after the care starts, so seven days means the care
-- continued to a day at least seven days after the day it started.
-- src:4136 | (ii) that care continues without interruption for a period of at least seven days beginning with the day after the day on which the care starts,
@ref s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) (src:4136)
GIVEN `the day the care started` IS A DATE
      `the last day of uninterrupted care` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) the care has continued without interruption for at least seven days` MEANS
    Day `the last day of uninterrupted care` MINUS Day `the day the care started` AT LEAST 7

-- (2)(b) "a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week".
-- src:4137 | (b) that the person has been in employed earner’s employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week,
@ref s 171ZZ16(2)(b) (src:4137)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` MEANS
    weeks AT LEAST 26

-- (2)(c) "at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7))".
-- src:4138 | (c) that at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7)), and
@ref s 171ZZ16(2)(c) (src:4138)
GIVEN `the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paragraph is omitted by subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraph is omitted by subsection (7)`
    WHEN JUST omitted THEN omitted OR `the person was entitled to be in that employment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the person was entitled to be in that employment`

-- (2)(d) "normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower
-- earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week".
-- src:4139 | (d) that the person’s normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week.
@ref s 171ZZ16(2)(d) (src:4139)
GIVEN `normal weekly earnings in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` MEANS
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds` AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`

-- (3) "Regulations may provide that a person is not entitled to pay in respect of a particular week or period of
-- consecutive weeks unless, at the beginning of that week or period (a) the person is in employed earner's employment with
-- the employer by reference to whom the condition in subsection (2)(b) is satisfied, and (b) that employment has been
-- continuous from the end of the relevant week."  If no regulations prescribe the condition there is none to fail.
-- src:4140 | (3) Regulations may provide that a person is not entitled to pay in respect of a particular week or period of consecutive weeks unless, at the beginning of that week or period—
-- src:4141 | (a) the person is in employed earner’s employment with the employer by reference to whom the condition in subsection (2)(b) is satisfied, and
-- src:4142 | (b) that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week.
@ref s 171ZZ16(3) (src:4140-4142)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- no condition has been prescribed under subsection (3), so there is none to fail
    ELSE IF `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment` AND `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is not entitled to pay in respect of a particular week or period of consecutive weeks unless, at the beginning of that week or period"

-- (4) "'neonatal care' means care (a) of a prescribed medical or palliative kind, and (b) that starts before the end of a
-- period of 28 days beginning with the day after the date of the child's birth."  That period runs from the day after the
-- birth to the 28th day after it, so care that starts on the 28th day after the birth starts before the period ends and care that
-- starts on the 29th does not.  (5): regulations may prescribe a kind of care by place -- a power, nothing to encode.
-- src:4143 | (4) For the purposes of this Part, “neonatal care” means care—
-- src:4144 | (a) of a prescribed medical or palliative kind, and
-- src:4145 | (b) that starts before the end of a period of 28 days beginning with the day after the date of the child’s birth.
@ref s 171ZZ16(4) (src:4143-4145)
GIVEN `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the care starts` IS A DATE
      `the date of the child's birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` MEANS
    IF     `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind`
       AND Day `the day the care starts` MINUS Day `the date of the child's birth` AT MOST 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“neonatal care” means care—" ... "of a prescribed medical or palliative kind, and" ... "that starts before the end of a period of 28 days beginning with the day after the date of the child’s birth"

-- (6) "In this section the 'relevant week' (a) in any case where the person is entitled to statutory maternity pay under
-- section 164 in respect of the child, is the week immediately preceding the 14th week before the expected week of
-- confinement (within the meaning of Part 12); (b) ... statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth) ... the same week as
-- the relevant week for the purposes of section 171ZA(2) in that case; (c) ... 171ZB (adoption) ... 171ZB(2); (d) ... statutory
-- adoption pay under section 171ZL ... 171ZL(2); (e) in any other case, is the week immediately before the one in which the
-- neonatal care starts."  The relevant weeks of ss 171ZA(2), 171ZB(2) and 171ZL(2) are other Parts' answers (seam S30), taken as
-- inputs.  "Expected week of confinement" is not defined in the text, so the week is asked as a fact.  If the person has more than
-- one of the entitlements (a) to (d) with different weeks, the text does not say which governs.  "Week" is a Sunday-start week
-- unless regulations prescribe another period (s 171ZZ24(5)).
-- src:4147 | (6) In this section the “relevant week”—
-- src:4148 | (a) in any case where the person is entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164 in respect of the child, is the week immediately preceding the 14th week before the expected week of confinement (within the meaning of Part 12);
-- src:4149 | (b) in any case where the person is entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth) in respect of the child, is the same week as the relevant week for the purposes of section 171ZA(2) in that case;
-- src:4150 | (c) in any case where the person is entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption) in respect of the child, is the same week as the relevant week for the purposes of section 171ZB(2) in that case;
-- src:4151 | (d) in any case where the person is entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL in respect of the child, is the same week as the relevant week for the purposes of section 171ZL(2) in that case;
-- src:4152 | (e) in any other case, is the week immediately before the one in which the neonatal care starts.
@ref s 171ZZ16(6) (src:4147-4152)
GIVEN entitlements IS A `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child`
      `the expected week of confinement` IS A Period
      `s 171ZA(2) the relevant week` IS A Period
      `s 171ZB(2) the relevant week` IS A Period
      `s 171ZL(2) the relevant week` IS A Period
      `the day the neonatal care starts` IS A DATE
      `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the person's case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZZ24(5) lets regulations prescribe "such other period" for the week
    ELSE CONSIDER (    (IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
                   PLUS (IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
                   PLUS (IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
                   PLUS (IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` THEN 1 ELSE 0))
         WHEN 0 THEN JUST (Period WITH
                              `the first day` IS Date (Day `the day the neonatal care starts` MINUS (`Weekday of` `the day the neonatal care starts`) MINUS 7)
                              `the last day`  IS Date (Day `the day the neonatal care starts` MINUS (`Weekday of` `the day the neonatal care starts`) MINUS 1))
         WHEN 1 THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164`
                 THEN JUST (Period WITH
                                `the first day` IS Date (Day (`the expected week of confinement`'s `the first day`) MINUS 105)
                                `the last day`  IS Date (Day (`the expected week of confinement`'s `the first day`) MINUS 99))
                 IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)`
                 THEN JUST `s 171ZA(2) the relevant week`
                 IF entitlements's `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)`
                 THEN JUST `s 171ZB(2) the relevant week`
                 OTHERWISE JUST `s 171ZL(2) the relevant week`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person is entitled under more than one of (a) to (d) and the text does not say which relevant week governs

-- (7) "In relation to neonatal care that starts before the day on which section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes
-- fully into force, subsection (2) above is to be read as if paragraph (c) were omitted."
-- src:4153 | (7) In relation to neonatal care that starts before the day on which section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force, subsection (2) above is to be read as if paragraph (c) were omitted.
@ref s 171ZZ16(7) (src:4153)
GIVEN `the day the neonatal care starts` IS A DATE
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` MEANS
    IF `the day the neonatal care starts` LESS THAN `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the omission is for care that "starts before the day"; later care is for (2)(c) itself

§§ `s 171ZZ17 Entitlement: supplementary`

-- (1) "A person is entitled to payments ... in respect of any period only if the person gives notice to whoever
-- is liable to make the payments stating the week or weeks in respect of which they are to be made."
-- Given the notice, the entitlement is whatever s 171ZZ16(1) says; without it the text says no.
-- src:4155 | (1) A person is entitled to payments of statutory neonatal care pay in respect of any period only if the person gives notice to whoever is liable to make the payments stating the week or weeks in respect of which they are to be made.
@ref s 171ZZ17(1) (src:4155)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under s 171ZZ16(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has given notice to whoever is liable, stating the weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` MEANS
    IF `the person has given notice to whoever is liable, stating the weeks`
    THEN `the person is entitled under s 171ZZ16(1)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to payments of statutory neonatal care pay in respect of any period only if the person gives notice"

-- (3) "The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay ... so requests."
-- src:4157 | (3) The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory neonatal care pay so requests.
@ref s 171ZZ17(3) (src:4157)
GIVEN `the person who is liable to pay has asked for the notice to be in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ17(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` MEANS
    IF `the person who is liable to pay has asked for the notice to be in writing` AND (NOT `the notice is in writing`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory neonatal care pay so requests."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ18 Liability to make payments`

-- (1) "The liability to make payments ... is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments
-- has been an employee as mentioned in subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section."
-- The list of persons is not closed: subsection (3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable instead.
-- src:4177 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory neonatal care pay under section 171ZZ16 is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section.
@ref s 171ZZ18(1) (src:4177)
GIVEN `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZZ16(2)(b) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ18(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory neonatal care pay` MEANS
    IF `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZZ16(2)(b) and (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the liability is "a liability of any person of whom" the entitled person has been an employee; s 171ZZ18(3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The text gives no time limit and no consequence of default, so none is invented.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ18 Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ18 the person liable to make the payments`

DECLARE `s 171ZZ18 Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ18 makes a payment of statutory neonatal care pay` HAS amount IS A NUMBER

-- src:4177 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory neonatal care pay under section 171ZZ16 is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section.
@ref s 171ZZ18(1) (src:4177)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 171ZZ18 Party` `s 171ZZ18 Action`
`s 171ZZ18(1) the duty to make the payments` MEANS
    PARTY `s 171ZZ18 the person liable to make the payments`
    MUST `s 171ZZ18 makes a payment of statutory neonatal care pay` amount
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `s 171ZZ19 Rate and period of pay`

-- (1) "payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations".  The Act gives no figure.
-- src:4181 | (1) Statutory neonatal care pay is payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations, which may prescribe different kinds of rate for different cases.
@ref s 171ZZ19(1) (src:4181)
GIVEN `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ19(1) the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the prescribed rate is not given

-- (2) "payable in respect of (a) such week within the qualifying period, or (b) such number of weeks, not exceeding the
-- prescribed number of weeks, within the qualifying period, as the person entitled may choose".
-- One week is a choice of one week.  A choice outside the limit (more weeks than the prescribed number, or weeks outside
-- the qualifying period) is outside the grant: the text does not say it is unpayable.
-- src:4182 | (2) Statutory neonatal care pay is payable in respect of—
-- src:4183 | (a) such week within the qualifying period, or
-- src:4184 | (b) such number of weeks, not exceeding the prescribed number of weeks, within the qualifying period,
-- src:4185 | as the person entitled may choose in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ19(2) (src:4182-4185)
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks chosen` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `all the weeks chosen are within the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` MEANS
    IF `all the weeks chosen are within the qualifying period` AND `the number of weeks chosen` AT MOST `the prescribed number of weeks`
    THEN JUST (`the weekly rate in pounds` TIMES `the number of weeks chosen`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant covers weeks "within the qualifying period" and a number "not exceeding the prescribed number of weeks"

-- (3) "Provision under subsection (2)(b) must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than 12."
-- src:4186 | (3) Provision under subsection (2)(b) must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than 12.
@ref s 171ZZ19(3) (src:4186)
GIVEN `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` MEANS
    IF `the prescribed number of weeks` AT LEAST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than 12"

-- (5) "the qualifying period is to be determined in accordance with regulations, which must secure that it is a period
-- of at least 68 weeks beginning with the date of the child's birth."  Both ends are counted; 68 weeks is 476 days.
-- src:4188 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), the qualifying period is to be determined in accordance with regulations, which must secure that it is a period of at least 68 weeks beginning with the date of the child’s birth.
@ref s 171ZZ19(5) (src:4188)
GIVEN qperiod IS A Period
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(5) the qualifying period is allowed` MEANS
    IF     qperiod's `the first day` EQUALS `the day the child was born`
       AND (Day (qperiod's `the last day`) MINUS Day (qperiod's `the first day`)) PLUS 1 AT LEAST 476
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must secure that it is a period of at least 68 weeks beginning with the date of the child's birth"

-- (6) "A person is not liable to pay statutory neonatal care pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week
-- during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person."
-- src:4189 | (6) A person is not liable to pay statutory neonatal care pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person.
@ref s 171ZZ19(6) (src:4189)
GIVEN `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` MEANS
    IF `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not liable to pay statutory neonatal care pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): liability for a week the other does not work is for s 171ZZ18, not this subsection

-- (7) "It is immaterial for the purposes of subsection (6) whether the work referred to in that subsection is work under a
-- contract of service which existed immediately before the statutory pay week or ... which did not so exist."
-- So the answer is the (6) answer whichever way the second fact falls.
-- src:4190 | (7) It is immaterial for the purposes of subsection (6) whether the work referred to in that subsection is work under a contract of service which existed immediately before the statutory pay week or a contract of service which did not so exist.
@ref s 171ZZ19(7) (src:4190)
GIVEN `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service existed immediately before the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` MEANS
    `s 171ZZ19(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week`
        `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week`

-- (8) "Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory neonatal care pay is not payable to a person in respect
-- of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person".
-- src:4191 | (8) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory neonatal care pay is not payable to a person in respect of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person statutory neonatal care pay.
@ref s 171ZZ19(8) (src:4191)
GIVEN `the person works during any part of the statutory pay week for an employer who is not liable to pay the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` MEANS
    IF `the case is one prescribed by regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `the person works during any part of the statutory pay week for an employer who is not liable to pay the person`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "statutory neonatal care pay is not payable to a person in respect of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a week without that work is for the grant in subsection (2)

-- (10) "the amount payable ... for any day is to be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate."
-- src:4193 | (10) Where for any purpose of this Part or of regulations it is necessary to calculate the daily rate of statutory neonatal care pay, the amount payable by way of statutory neonatal care pay for any day is to be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate.
@ref s 171ZZ19(10) (src:4193)
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ19(10) the daily rate in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate in pounds` DIVIDED BY 7

-- (11) "'statutory pay week' ... means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which
-- statutory neonatal care pay is to be payable; 'week' means any period of seven days."  The week convention is the core's
-- `any period of 7 days`.  Both ends of the period are counted.
-- src:4194 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4195 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory neonatal care pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory neonatal care pay is to be payable;
-- src:4196 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ19(11) (src:4194-4196)
GIVEN period IS A Period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a week` MEANS
    (Day (period's `the last day`) MINUS Day (period's `the first day`)) PLUS 1 EQUALS 7

-- src:4194 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4195 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory neonatal care pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory neonatal care pay is to be payable;
-- src:4196 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ19(11) (src:4194-4196)
GIVEN period IS A Period
      `the person chose the week as a week in respect of which the pay is to be payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a statutory pay week` MEANS
    `the person chose the week as a week in respect of which the pay is to be payable` AND `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a week` period

-- src:4194 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4195 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory neonatal care pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory neonatal care pay is to be payable;
-- src:4196 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ19(11) (src:4194-4196)
`s 171ZZ19(11) the week convention` MEANS `any period of 7 days`

§§ `s 171ZZ20 Restrictions on contracting out`

-- (1) "An agreement is void to the extent that it purports (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of
-- this Part, or (b) to require a person to contribute ... towards any costs incurred by that person's employer or former
-- employer under this Part."  An agreement that purports neither is not said to be void here.
-- src:4198 | (1) An agreement is void to the extent that it purports—
-- src:4199 | (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of this Part, or
-- src:4200 | (b) to require a person to contribute (whether directly or indirectly) towards any costs incurred by that person’s employer or former employer under this Part.
@ref s 171ZZ20(1) (src:4198-4200)
GIVEN `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ20(1) the agreement is void to that extent` MEANS
    IF `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part`
       OR `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "void to the extent that it purports" (a) or (b); an agreement that purports neither is not covered by this subsection

-- (2) "An agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising any deductions from
-- statutory neonatal care pay ..., is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make
-- the same deductions from any contractual remuneration ..., or (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to
-- pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period."  A failed "if" is counted as the text's no (reading (a)).
-- src:4201 | (2) An agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising any deductions from statutory neonatal care pay which the employer is liable to pay to the employee in respect of any period, is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer—
-- src:4202 | (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from any contractual remuneration which the employer is liable to pay in respect of the same period, or
-- src:4203 | (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ20(2) (src:4201-4203)
GIVEN `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ20(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration`
       OR `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer" is authorised, or would be (a failed "if"; reading (a))

§§ `s 171ZZ21 Relationship with contractual remuneration`

-- (1) "Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory neonatal care pay does not affect any right
-- of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service ('contractual remuneration')."
-- Subsection (3) lets regulations decide which payments are contractual remuneration, so if they say otherwise the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4205 | (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory neonatal care pay does not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
@ref s 171ZZ21(1) (src:4205)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ21(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` MEANS
    IF `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (3) lets regulations say which payments are, and which are not, contractual remuneration
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any entitlement to statutory neonatal care pay does not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service"

-- (2)(a) "any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer ... in respect of any period is to go towards
-- discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory neonatal care pay to that person in respect of that period".
-- The remuneration paid is net of anything regulations treat as not being contractual remuneration (subsection (3)).
-- src:4207 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer of that person in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory neonatal care pay to that person in respect of that period; and
@ref s 171ZZ21(2)(a) (src:4207)
GIVEN `liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ21(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay that remains` MEANS
    IF `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay for the period, in pounds` MINUS `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds`

-- (2)(b) "any statutory neonatal care pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in
-- respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration".
-- src:4208 | (b) any statutory neonatal care pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to that person in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ21(2)(b) (src:4208)
GIVEN `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `statutory neonatal care pay paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ21(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` MEANS
    IF `statutory neonatal care pay paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` MINUS `statutory neonatal care pay paid for the same period, in pounds`

§§ `s 171ZZ22 Crown employment`

-- "The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to
-- persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown."  The answer is the same whoever the employer is.
-- src:4211 | The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown.
@ref s 171ZZ22 (src:4211)
GIVEN `the kind of employer` IS A `Kind of employer`
      `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of employer`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a company or other body corporate` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `the Crown` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`

§§ `s 171ZZ23 Special classes of person`

-- (1) "The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part
-- ... in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or
-- aircraft; (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or (c) in prescribed
-- employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2)."
-- This is what the power reaches; the regulations themselves are outside the sources (subsection (2) lists what they may do).
-- src:4213 | (1) The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks proper in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be—
-- src:4214 | (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft;
-- src:4215 | (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or
-- src:4216 | (c) in prescribed employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2).
@ref s 171ZZ23(1) (src:4213-4216)
GIVEN `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in prescribed employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft`
        OR `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances`
        OR (`the person is in prescribed employment` AND `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for a person who is, has been or is to be in one of the three classes

§§ `s 171ZZ24 Supplementary`

-- Nouns for the kinds of change that "modifications" names.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ24(1) kind of change` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ24(1) an addition`
    `s 171ZZ24(1) an omission`
    `s 171ZZ24(1) an amendment`
    `s 171ZZ24(1) another kind of change`

-- (1) "'employer', in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who (first limb) under section 6 is liable to
-- pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee, or (second limb)
-- would be liable to pay such contributions but for (A) the condition in section 6(1)(b), or (B) the employee being under
-- the age of 16."  The limb labels are not in the converter text; "first limb", "second limb", "(A)" and "(B)" are mine.
-- src:4224 | “employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who—
-- src:4225 | under section 6 is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee, or
-- src:4226 | would be liable to pay such contributions but for—
-- src:4227 | the condition in section 6(1)(b), or
-- src:4228 | the employee being under the age of 16;
@ref s 171ZZ24(1) (src:4224-4228)
GIVEN `s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to earnings of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 6 the person would be liable but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 6 the person would be liable but for the employee being under 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` MEANS
    IF     `s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to earnings of the employee`
        OR `s 6 the person would be liable but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `s 6 the person would be liable but for the employee being under 16`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who" is liable, or would be but for the condition or the age
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 173(a) the person is under 16`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 173(a) does not answer whether the employee is under 16
              WHEN JUST under16 THEN
                  IF under16 THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who" would be liable "but for ... the employee being under the age of 16"; the employee is not under 16

-- (1) "'modifications' includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly".
-- src:4229 | “modifications” includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly;
@ref s 171ZZ24(1) (src:4229)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 171ZZ24(1) kind of change`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ24(1) the change is a modification` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 171ZZ24(1) an addition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ24(1) an omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ24(1) an amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ24(1) another kind of change` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes additions, omissions and amendments" does not close the list

-- (1) "'prescribed' means prescribed by regulations".
-- src:4230 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ24(1) (src:4230)
GIVEN `the matter is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ24(1) the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    IF `the matter is prescribed by regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed by regulations"

-- (2) "In this Part, 'employee' means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of
-- service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings (within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5)."
-- "Gainfully" is read as adding nothing to "with earnings" (fork in NOTES).  Whether the person has "earnings" in that
-- sense is a borrowed fact.  Whether adjacent waters count as Great Britain (s 172(a)) is already in the core's field.
-- src:4231 | (2) In this Part, “employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings (within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5).
@ref s 171ZZ24(2) (src:4231)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the person has earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` MEANS
    IF     employment's `carried on in Great Britain`
       AND (employment's `held under a contract of service` OR employment's `held in an office`)
       AND `the person has earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings"

-- (5) "In this Part, except section 171ZZ19, 'week' means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as
-- may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases."  The core's fifth week convention.
-- src:4238 | (5) In this Part, except section 171ZZ19, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZZ24(5) (src:4238)
`s 171ZZ24(5) the week convention` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`

-- src:4238 | (5) In this Part, except section 171ZZ19, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZZ24(5) (src:4238)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 171ZZ24(5) the first day of the week containing the day` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other period as may be prescribed"
    ELSE JUST (Date (Day day MINUS (`Weekday of` day)))

-- (6) "a person's normal weekly earnings are, subject to subsection (8), to be taken to be the average weekly earnings which
-- in the relevant period have been paid to the person or paid for the person's benefit under the contract of service with
-- the employer in question."  (7): "earnings" and "relevant period" are whatever regulations say, so the total and the
-- number of weeks are inputs.  (8): in prescribed cases regulations calculate it, so the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4239 | (6) For the purposes of this Part, a person’s normal weekly earnings are, subject to subsection (8), to be taken to be the average weekly earnings which in the relevant period have been paid to the person or paid for the person’s benefit under the contract of service with the employer in question.
-- src:4240 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6), “earnings” and “relevant period” have the meanings given to them by regulations.
-- src:4241 | (8) In such cases as may be prescribed, a person’s normal weekly earnings are to be calculated in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ24(6) (src:4239-4241)
GIVEN `the earnings paid in the relevant period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations prescribe another calculation in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ24(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another calculation in the case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (8), "In such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `the number of weeks in the relevant period` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN JUST (`the earnings paid in the relevant period, in pounds` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in the relevant period`)
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an average over a relevant period with no weeks is not defined

